<http://www.spektrix.com/persephonetheatre/event/40201AJMHGMLBHTGVNKHNPGVSVHHPSMBQ>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Tilda Swinton Betrayed Us & Dungeness";
  schema:description """
	Persephone Theatre’s Young Company presents:<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">Tilda Swinton Betrayed Us</span></span> <span class=\"BoldText\">by A. Rey Pamatmat</span><span><br/></span>The survival of actress Tilda Swinton’s biggest fan club is threatened when the actions of their beloved icon leave the group sharply divided. <span class=\"ItalicText\">Tilda Swinton Betrayed Us</span> is a play talking about the difficult and complicated things that we often don’t want to talk about.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">Dungeness</span></span> <span class=\"BoldText\">by Chris Thompson</span><span><br/></span>In a place where nothing ever happens, a group of teenagers share a safe house for 2SLGBTQ+ youth. The group must decide how they want to commemorate an attack that happened to people like them in a country far away. How do you make a decision when none of you can agree on anything? How do you protest if you’re not ready to tell the world who you are? <span class=\"ItalicText\">Dungeness</span> is a play about love, commemoration and protest.
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-03-19T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/persephonetheatre/files/4ba2c4e1-036b-4afa-aae1-2138e45f3ab9.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/persephonetheatre/location/604AGRPTGQTTPRPKPVCQNNLBRGTLVJRBR>;
  schema:offers _:a9a424fcb3ab475ea2103afc11b5c6ad297;
  schema:duration "PT60M";
  schema:endDate "2026-03-19T20:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

_:a9a424fcb3ab475ea2103afc11b5c6ad297 a schema:AggregateOffer;
  schema:lowPrice "8.5";
  schema:priceCurrency "CAD" .

<http://www.spektrix.com/persephonetheatre/event/40401AJTHBLMVMBVCCLGRTCHHQHMCLTQK>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Tilda Swinton Betrayed Us & Dungeness";
  schema:description """
	Persephone Theatre’s Young Company presents:<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">Tilda Swinton Betrayed Us</span></span> <span class=\"BoldText\">by A. Rey Pamatmat</span><span><br/></span>The survival of actress Tilda Swinton’s biggest fan club is threatened when the actions of their beloved icon leave the group sharply divided. <span class=\"ItalicText\">Tilda Swinton Betrayed Us</span> is a play talking about the difficult and complicated things that we often don’t want to talk about.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">Dungeness</span></span> <span class=\"BoldText\">by Chris Thompson</span><span><br/></span>In a place where nothing ever happens, a group of teenagers share a safe house for 2SLGBTQ+ youth. The group must decide how they want to commemorate an attack that happened to people like them in a country far away. How do you make a decision when none of you can agree on anything? How do you protest if you’re not ready to tell the world who you are? <span class=\"ItalicText\">Dungeness</span> is a play about love, commemoration and protest.
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-03-20T12:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
