<http://www.spektrix.com/persephonetheatre/event/3668AJHTVQKTPGSNGJQBSQSHSGDRCVLQP>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Where the Wild Things Are (Public Shows)";
  schema:description """
	A Presentation House Theatre production⁠<span><br/></span>Based on the book by Maurice Sendak and originally adapted for the stage by TAG Theatre Glasgow, Scotland⁠<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Recommended Audience: 3 plus<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Sail away to the land of the Wild Things! Jump in and help Max transform his bedroom into an exotic jungle, then transport yourself to where the wild things are. After being crowned king of these magical creatures, Max must make a decision: stay and rule the Wild Things or return home. Together, young ones and their adults can join this wild rumpus – based on the timeless children’s book, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Where the Wild Things Are</span> by Maurice Sendak.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>This production of <span class=\"ItalicText\">Where the Wild Things Are</span> is an interactive experience. Audience members will be seated around the performance area on three large mats, with limited chairs provided at the back for grownups who may require a seat.
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-03-07T10:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
